 "name": "engineers",
 "who": "Software engineers. They read code daily, run things from a terminal, and review each other's changes. They know general industry vocabulary but not your product's or your infrastructure's.",
 "_note": "A BASELINE: no `matches`, so it never applies on its own. Audiences inherit it. This is where the tool's bias lives, and it is deliberate \u2014 it targets engineers. Other baselines are welcome as data files beside this one; nothing in the code knows this name except the configured default for an unresolved audience. The system word list is the 1913 web2 dictionary and has no modern computing vocabulary, so words like INLINE and KUBECTL were being reported as unexplained jargon. Those live here.",
